      "writtenOn": "2025-03-31T20:59:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"wouldn\u0027t we still be compiling a valid pipeline w/ a compatible renderpass for the eventual real rendering scenario of a DrawList with all draws not requiring dst reads?\"\n\nYes - the problem is how we currently handle serializing and deserializing android-style keys for precompilation. We want to maintain a renderpassdesc\u0027s dst read strategy across packing/unpacking keys so we can populate a real value (using kNone triggers ShaderInfo assertions that if a dst read is required we provide a strategy that isn\u0027t `kNoneRequired` - I could look into changing that assert for precompilation use cases as one possible change) but do not actually care whether they match.\nSo when real-world versus precompilation keys are compared for equality, we fail the `UserDefinedStableKeyTest`.\n\nAnyhow, sending out the beginning of some responses - marking CL as WIP while I test out one path forward (always assigning a dst read strategy for RenderPassDesc used for precompilation, removing dst read strategy from renderpassdesc serialization, removing TextureInfo as arg for caps-\u003egetDstReadStrategy, and calling caps-\u003egetDstReadStrategy when it\u0027s time to recreate the RenderPassDesc from keys). Wanted to get some replies out as an update.",
      "parentUuid": "1eba7ea6_f7a15948",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 209,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 211,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "57c02efdc9462ce955f8339cc46ce5727a88bfb5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
