      "writtenOn": "2025-03-31T20:59:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this occurred to me as well. Thinking about the best point to do this...\nI am wanting to land these changes with the above `#ifdef`, with an immediate plan to remove them once the necessary precompilation changes are made (that can be independent of this CL chain).\n\nSo, so long as we keep this check outside of the `#ifdef` for the precompilation workaround, I agree `TextureInfo` could be removed now / in a direct follow-up CL to this one. That does rely us leaning on the fact that only Vulkan uses `kReadFromInput` (or more precisely, that any backend that does use it also cannot use that strategy on MSAA textures), but we already tie this strategy to a particular backend anyhow in shader compilation (in a later CL) which folks seemed OK with, so I can live with that.\n\nWill add follow-on CL to remove that.",
